[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2739113756","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104379#issuecomment-2739113756","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104379","id":2739113756,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6jQ48c","user":{"login":"etherealxx","id":64251396,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MjUxMzk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64251396?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etherealxx","html_url":"https://github.com/etherealxx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etherealxx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etherealxx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etherealxx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etherealxx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etherealxx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etherealxx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etherealxx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etherealxx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etherealxx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-20T04:26:44Z","updated_at":"2025-03-20T04:26:44Z","body":"I agree that this is a breaking change. While it's still possible to get the path from the UID, it's counterintuitive since the Inspector UI display the path when it's actually an uid path. Some of my functions that expect string path is broken.\n\nAlso if you're having an exported array of file paths from a 4.3 project, and upgrading to 4.4, the existing array items will still be file path, while if you add a new one from inspector, it'll be an UID path. So there's two different type of path in a single exported variable.\n\nMy suggested solution (aside from that new parameter, if it's possible) would be a project setting that decide the default behavior of @export_file, either using UID path or the regular string path. And probably make a new one (@export_uid or something) that always return UID path for those who prefers that","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2739113756/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2739123788","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104379#issuecomment-2739123788","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104379","id":2739123788,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6jQ7ZM","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-20T04:34:48Z","updated_at":"2025-03-20T04:34:48Z","body":"In my opinion, we should restore the old behavior (for compatibility and consistency reasons) and not introduce an annotation parameter (since it is incompatible) or a project setting (since it is error-prone). Instead, we could add a new dedicated export hint and annotation `@export_file_as_uid`, `@export_file_uid` or `@export_uid`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2739123788/reactions","total_count":10,"+1":10,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2739138161","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104379#issuecomment-2739138161","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104379","id":2739138161,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6jQ-5x","user":{"login":"etherealxx","id":64251396,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MjUxMzk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64251396?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etherealxx","html_url":"https://github.com/etherealxx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etherealxx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etherealxx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etherealxx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etherealxx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etherealxx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etherealxx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etherealxx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etherealxx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etherealxx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-20T04:44:49Z","updated_at":"2025-03-20T04:44:49Z","body":"@dalexeev but what about those who are new with 4.4 and already used to the new method? That's another breaking change for them, if the change is supposed to be in a patch (4.4.x) update.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2739138161/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2739148251","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104379#issuecomment-2739148251","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104379","id":2739148251,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6jRBXb","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-20T04:53:54Z","updated_at":"2025-03-20T04:53:54Z","body":"I think it's better to break for a small number of new users (4.4 was released very recently) and it's unlikely that UID -> path will break anyone's expectations as much as path -> UID. Excessive configurability is bad, in my opinion the behavior of `@export_file` should be the same for all projects, regardless of the project settings.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2739148251/reactions","total_count":8,"+1":8,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2746369833","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104379#issuecomment-2746369833","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104379","id":2746369833,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6jskcp","user":{"login":"geekley","id":38332912,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4MzMyOTEy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38332912?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley","html_url":"https://github.com/geekley","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-23T19:04:45Z","updated_at":"2025-03-23T19:04:45Z","body":"> I think it's better to break for a small number of new users (4.4 was released very recently) and it's unlikely that UID -> path will break anyone's expectations as much as path -> UID. Excessive configurability is bad, in my opinion the behavior of `@export_file` should be the same for all projects, regardless of the project settings.\n\nOh if this can be done, that's even better IMO! I have zero issues with that.\n\nNew annotation for uid is the best choice, I just suggested config because I was assuming you can't \"counter-break\" it. I suppose you can at least in 4.5; dunno about 4.4.1 (on one hand you shouldn't change behavior on a patch, on the other it would be best to reverse it fast enough that's still \"a small number of new users\", plus if going by the docs, the 4.4 behavior is technically \"wrong\"/not-as-documented anyway...?)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2746369833/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2746647760","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104379#issuecomment-2746647760","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104379","id":2746647760,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6jtoTQ","user":{"login":"hakuhan","id":18411187,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDExMTg3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18411187?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hakuhan","html_url":"https://github.com/hakuhan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hakuhan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hakuhan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hakuhan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hakuhan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hakuhan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hakuhan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hakuhan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hakuhan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hakuhan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-24T01:24:20Z","updated_at":"2025-03-24T01:24:54Z","body":"Can we get the original file path by uuid? Maybe it is better to provide a method whitch returns file path by uuid then I can check path again.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2746647760/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2746669740","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104379#issuecomment-2746669740","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104379","id":2746669740,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6jttqs","user":{"login":"geekley","id":38332912,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4MzMyOTEy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38332912?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley","html_url":"https://github.com/geekley","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-24T01:46:54Z","updated_at":"2025-03-24T01:46:54Z","body":"I'm not sure if you can (without actually loading it from uid to get its resource_path), but even if so, that still wouldn't unbreak it for use cases where you purposely DON'T want refactoring to apply.\n\nSometimes I might actually want it to be that path, even if I break or move the actual pointed file around. The same way I don't always necessarily want refactoring to update references automatically if I rename a class in JS code for example.\n\nSo I think the ideal is really having 2 annotations, and making sure the docs of `@export_file` point people to prefer using the uid version in most typical use cases because it follows refactoring, but still leave previous behavior intact for those who need it in special use cases.\n\nI mean, if you want it to be so bound that refactoring would apply, often you might as well `@export` the resource directly instead of its path/uid. But I see valid use cases for all 3 scenarios.\n\nSide note: one of the very reasons I moved away from Unity into Godot was the way asset identity is tightly tied to its path, not based on an AssetDatabase like Unity. Just like in code classes/namespaces, it forces you to think in a more organized way, and I see that as an absolutely good thing, as long as refactoring works at least on most cases.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2746669740/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2768444695","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104379#issuecomment-2768444695","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104379","id":2768444695,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lAx0X","user":{"login":"Summersay415","id":71974498,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxOTc0NDk4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71974498?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Summersay415","html_url":"https://github.com/Summersay415","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Summersay415/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Summersay415/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Summersay415/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Summersay415/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Summersay415/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Summersay415/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Summersay415/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Summersay415/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Summersay415/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-01T07:31:10Z","updated_at":"2025-04-01T07:31:10Z","body":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/91815 was good PR for splitting these things, but yeah, it's closed","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2768444695/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2785071871","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104379#issuecomment-2785071871","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104379","id":2785071871,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mANL_","user":{"login":"nanoquack","id":435471,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNTQ3MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/435471?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nanoquack","html_url":"https://github.com/nanoquack","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nanoquack/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nanoquack/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nanoquack/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nanoquack/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nanoquack/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nanoquack/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nanoquack/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nanoquack/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nanoquack/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-08T02:31:03Z","updated_at":"2025-04-10T23:27:55Z","body":"In order to quickly make the change for a project going from 4.3 to 4.4, would there be any issue using e.g. `@export_custom(PROPERTY_HINT_FILE, \"*.tscn\")` as a quick fix if you need the file path instead of the uid string?\n\nEdit 1: `@export_custom(PROPERTY_HINT_FILE, \"*.tscn\")` also sets the file path as uid, so the only quick fix for now seems to be to use `@export`\n\nEdit2: As a relatively simple workaround for now: Implement a custom EditorInspectorPlugin and EditorProperty which sets the property to the real file path as a quick fix for now\n\n\n> In my opinion, we should restore the old behavior (for compatibility and consistency reasons) and not introduce an annotation parameter (since it is incompatible) or a project setting (since it is error-prone). Instead, we could add a new dedicated export hint and annotation `@export_file_as_uid`, `@export_file_uid` or `@export_uid`.\n\nSounds like a good plan!\n\nAs an (important) aside: I am an avid fan of Godot, but changes made in a way like this one make me sometimes worry what else can unexpectedly break compatibility when upgrading between minor versions, because:\n\n- It's a big, obvious breaking change in a minor version where changes usually should be backwards compatible\n- The change is undocumented, its consequences not even immediately felt, but later when setting the property in the editor\n- While editing, inspector shows file path set, but during debugging inspector shows uid\n- Setting property by inspector changes file path to uid, setting property by code keeps file path","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2785071871/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2804296141","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104379#issuecomment-2804296141","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104379","id":2804296141,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6nJinN","user":{"login":"TokisanGames","id":632766,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzMjc2Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/632766?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokisanGames","html_url":"https://github.com/TokisanGames","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokisanGames/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokisanGames/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokisanGames/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokisanGames/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokisanGames/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokisanGames/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokisanGames/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokisanGames/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokisanGames/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-15T08:45:20Z","updated_at":"2025-04-18T10:49:55Z","body":"Yes, this breaking change to the behavior of @export_file should be completely reverted. Not flags, options or additional documentation. My team lost work because of this engine bug.\n\nI added `@export_file var scene_file: String : set = set_scene_file` because I want a file name in a string, and I want a file selector in the inspector. I don't want a UID in script. I can't imagine what I would do with it. \n\nNot only that, it doesn't even work properly. I'm using the filename to write to files, and using the UID instead of the filename failed to save data, without any notice. The data just disappeared.\n\nReading through #97912, it was intentional to store the UID, but clearly an oversight to break @export_file and not return the file name string as it does in the inspector. Clearly the UID is useless in the inspector so it returns the filename. It's just as useless in script. What should happen now to close the ticket is also return the filename via code (the old behavior).\n\nHere's how I'm working around it, by replacing the UID every time I use the variable so that Godot never tries to use the UID to write files.\n\n```gdscript\nfunc _validate_filename():\n\tif scene_file.begins_with(\"uid://\"):\n\t\tif ResourceLoader.exists(scene_file):\n\t\t\tvar path: String = ResourceUID.get_id_path(ResourceUID.text_to_id(scene_file))\n\t\t\tprint(\"Resetting UID: %s to file path: %s\" % [scene_file, path])\n\t\t\tscene_file = path\n\t\telse:\n\t\t\tpush_error(\"Scene file is a uid, but the UID doesn't exist: \", scene_file)\n```\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2804296141/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2804343905","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104379#issuecomment-2804343905","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104379","id":2804343905,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6nJuRh","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-15T09:01:05Z","updated_at":"2025-04-15T09:01:05Z","body":"> using the UID instead of the filename prevented saving data, without any notice.\n\n`ResourceSaver.save()` returns Error that you should handle. Using UID is not the only reason it can fail.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2804343905/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2804369372","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104379#issuecomment-2804369372","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104379","id":2804369372,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6nJ0fc","user":{"login":"TokisanGames","id":632766,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzMjc2Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/632766?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokisanGames","html_url":"https://github.com/TokisanGames","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokisanGames/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokisanGames/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokisanGames/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokisanGames/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokisanGames/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokisanGames/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokisanGames/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokisanGames/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokisanGames/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-15T09:09:48Z","updated_at":"2025-04-15T09:09:48Z","body":"`ResourceSaver.save()` did not print any errors to the console. In this case, attempting to write to the UID as the file name was the only reason it failed and was resolved when changing the name back to a string file name.\n\nYou're right that I should handle any returned error. Checking now, saving with a UID reports `ERR_FILE_UNRECOGNIZED = 15 File: Unrecognized error.`\n\nNevertheless, my comments stand. The behavior of @export_file should be reverted to automatically convert back to a filename just as the inspector does. And maybe ResourceSaver.save() fixed so it can handle UIDs, but this is less necessary if the filenames work.\n\n\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2804369372/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]